argentum.options.render_distance.tooltip=The render distance controls how far away terrain will be rendered. Shorter distances mean that less terrain will be rendered improving frame rates.
argentum.options.brightness.tooltip=Controls the brightness (gamma) of the game.
options.chunks=%s Chunks

argentum.options.gui_scale.tooltip=Sets the maximum scale factor to be used for the user interface. If 'auto' is used then the largest scale factor will always be used.
argentum.options.fullscreen.tooltip=If enabled the game will display in full-screen (if supported).
argentum.options.framerate_limit.tooltip=Controls the maximum frame rate. VSync synchronizes frames to the display's refresh rate for smoother presentation but may add input latency. A fixed limit can reduce power usage and system load.
options.framerate=%s fps

argentum.options.view_bobbing.tooltip=If enabled the player's view will sway and bob when moving around. Players who experience motion sickness while playing can benefit from disabling this.

argentum.options.graphics.tooltip=The default graphics quality controls some legacy options and is necessary for mod compatibility. If the options below are left to Default they will use this setting.
argentum.options.anaglyph.tooltip=Renders red/cyan stereoscopic output.

argentum.options.clouds.tooltip=Controls the presence of rendered clouds in the sky.
argentum.options.particles.tooltip=Controls the maximum number of particles which can be present on screen at any one time.
argentum.options.smooth_lighting.tooltip=Controls whether blocks will be smoothly lit and shaded. This slightly increases the amount of time needed to re-build a chunk but doesn't affect frame rates.
argentum.options.biome_blend.name=Biome Blend
argentum.options.biome_blend.tooltip=Controls the range which biomes will be sampled for block colorization. Higher values greatly increase the amount of time it takes to build chunks for diminishing improvements in quality.
sodium.options.biome_blend.value=%s blocks
argentum.options.chunk_fade_in_duration.name=Chunk Fade-In Duration
argentum.options.chunk_fade_in_duration.value=%s ms
argentum.options.chunk_fade_in_duration.tooltip=Controls how long it takes for newly loaded chunks to fully appear. Longer durations create a smoother transition between unloaded and loaded chunks, reducing visual popping, but may make distant terrain appear to 'fade in' more slowly.
sodium.options.entity_shadows.tooltip=If enabled basic shadows will be rendered beneath mobs and other entities.
argentum.options.mipmap_levels.tooltip=Controls the number of mipmaps which will be used for block model textures. Higher values provide better rendering of blocks in the distance but may adversely affect performance with many animated textures.

sodium.options.chunk_update_threads.name=Chunk Update Threads
sodium.options.chunk_update_threads.tooltip=Specifies the number of threads to use for chunk building. Using more threads can speed up chunk loading and update speed but may negatively impact frame times.
sodium.options.always_defer_chunk_updates.name=Always Defer Chunk Updates
sodium.options.always_defer_chunk_updates.tooltip=If enabled rendering will never wait for chunk updates to finish even if they are important. This can greatly improve frame rates in some scenarios but it may create significant visual lag in the world.
argentum.options.async_graph_search.name=Async Occlusion Culling
argentum.options.async_graph_search.tooltip=Performs occlusion/frustum culling asynchronously, up to one frame behind the current camera position. This can improve frametimes, particularly at higher render distances, but at the cost of chunks popping into view if the camera is turned too aggressively.

sodium.options.use_block_face_culling.name=Use Block Face Culling
sodium.options.use_block_face_culling.tooltip=If enabled only the sides of blocks which are facing the camera will be submitted for rendering. This can eliminate a large number of block faces very early in the rendering process saving memory bandwidth and time on the GPU. Some resource packs may have issues with this option so try disabling it if you're seeing holes in blocks.
sodium.options.use_fog_occlusion.name=Use Fog Occlusion
sodium.options.use_fog_occlusion.tooltip=If enabled chunks which are determined to be fully hidden by fog effects will not be rendered helping to improve performance. The improvement can be more dramatic when fog effects are heavier (such as while underwater) but it may cause undesirable visual artifacts between the sky and fog in some scenarios.
sodium.options.use_entity_culling.name=Use Entity Culling
sodium.options.use_entity_culling.tooltip=If enabled entities determined not to be in any visible chunks will be skipped during rendering. This can help improve performance by avoiding the rendering of entities located underground or behind walls.
argentum.options.entity_occlusion_interval.name=Entity Occlusion Interval
argentum.options.entity_occlusion_interval.tooltip=Specifies the minimum delay between visibility checks for each entity. Lower values can cull hidden entities sooner but increase CPU and GPU overhead, while higher values reduce overhead at the cost of entities remaining visible longer after moving behind walls.
argentum.options.particle_culling.name=Particle Culling
argentum.options.particle_culling.tooltip=If enabled particles outside the camera frustum or hidden behind terrain will be skipped during rendering. This can improve performance in particle-heavy scenes, but may cause particles to disappear unexpectedly with some mods.

argentum.options.entity_instancing.name=Entity Instancing
argentum.options.entity_instancing.tooltip=If enabled compatible entity models will be batched into instanced draw calls. This can significantly improve performance when many similar entities are visible, but may cause rendering issues with mods that use unusual entity renderers.
sodium.options.animate_only_visible_textures.name=Animate Only Visible Textures
sodium.options.animate_only_visible_textures.tooltip=If enabled only animated textures determined to be visible will be updated. This can provide a significant boost to frame rates on some hardware especially with heavier resource packs. If you experience issues with some textures not being animated try disabling this option.
argentum.options.font_batching.name=Font Batching
argentum.options.font_batching.tooltip=If enabled text rendering will be batched into fewer draw calls, improving performance when rendering large amounts of text.
sodium.options.translucent_face_sorting.name=Translucent Face Sorting
sodium.options.translucent_face_sorting.tooltip=If enabled translucent effects from surfaces such as stained glass and water will be applied correctly.
embeddium.options.use_faster_clouds.name=Use Faster Clouds
embeddium.options.use_faster_clouds.tooltip=When enabled, Argentum replaces vanilla cloud rendering with a less glitchy and potentially faster implementation. Disable this if mods' cloud customizations aren't visible.
argentum.options.safe_chunk_edges.name=Safe Chunk Edges
argentum.options.safe_chunk_edges.tooltip=If enabled chunks will wait for their neighbors before building edge geometry. This prevents temporary gaps and incorrect lighting at chunk borders, but reduces the effective server view distance by one chunk. Disable this on low-view-distance servers if the lost terrain matters.
sodium.options.use_compact_vertex_format.name=Use Compact Vertex Format
sodium.options.use_compact_vertex_format.tooltip=If enabled a more compact vertex format will be used for rendering chunks. This can reduce graphics memory usage and bandwidth requirements significantly especially for integrated graphics cards but can cause z-fighting with some resource packs due to how it reduces the precision of position and texture coordinate attributes.

sodium.options.cpu_render_ahead_limit.name=CPU Render-Ahead Limit
sodium.options.cpu_render_ahead_limit.tooltip=Specifies the maximum number of frames the CPU can be waiting on the GPU to finish rendering. Very low or high values may create frame rate instability.
sodium.options.cpu_render_ahead_limit.value=%s frame(s)

argentum.options.check_gl_errors.name=OpenGL Error Checks
argentum.options.check_gl_errors.tooltip=Checks for OpenGL errors during the game loop. Useful for debugging, but slower.

